NoJIT option: run only code from the AOT image (FEX 14c9268, on top of 0007)

On iOS without a debugger attached, memory can never be made executable.
With NoJIT=1 FEX does not ask for it:

- JIT code buffers are allocated read+write only; nothing runs from them.
- ContextImpl::CompileBlock stops FEX with an error naming the guest block
  when a block is not in the lookup cache, i.e. not in the AOT image,
  instead of compiling it.
- The dispatcher must come from the AOT image (patch 0006); if the image
  has none matching this build, FEX stops instead of making its own
  dispatcher executable.

